    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Simple vs Weighted Average</h2>
      <p>A simple average treats every number the same. A weighted average lets each number count according to how important it is, which is how most course grades, GPAs and price averages are worked out.</p>
      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table class="table">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Simple and weighted averages of the same scores</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Assessment</th><th scope="col">Score</th><th scope="col">Weight</th><th scope="col">Contribution</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Assignments</td><td>90</td><td>30%</td><td>27</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Midterm</td><td>80</td><td>50%</td><td>40</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Quizzes</td><td>70</td><td>20%</td><td>14</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>Simple average 80</td><td>100%</td><td><strong>Weighted 81</strong></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>The weighted result is higher because the strongest score (90) carries more weight than the weakest (70).</p>

      <h2>Where Weighted Averages Are Used</h2>
      <ul class="content-list">
        <li><strong>Grades:</strong> coursework, midterm and final exam weights from a syllabus. For grades by letter, the <a href="/tools/grade-calculator/">grade calculator</a> and <a href="/tools/gpa-calculator/">GPA calculator</a> do this with credit hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Average cost:</strong> if you buy 10 units at 5 and 30 units at 6, the average price is (50 + 180) ÷ 40 = 5.75, not 5.50.</li>
        <li><strong>Admissions:</strong> merit and aggregate formulas weight school results and entry tests; the <a href="/tools/merit-calculator/">merit calculator</a> handles marks out of different totals.</li>
        <li><strong>Statistics:</strong> price indexes such as the Consumer Price Index weight each category by its share of household spending.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>All calculations run in your browser. You can share a link that reopens your exact rows.</p>
    </section>
